 |\\n| `kv_payload_bytes` | Active encoded KV payload bytes, including raw fallback payloads. |\\n| `kv_h2d_bytes` | Sum of bytes actually submitted to H2D copies, including routing metadata, alignment and any additional rows/entries copied. This is not physical link-protocol traffic. |\\n| `kv_compression_ratio` | `sum(kv_raw_bytes) / sum(kv_payload_bytes)`. |\\n| `kv_transfer_ratio` | `sum(kv_raw_bytes) / sum(kv_h2d_bytes)`. |\\n| `kvload_ms` | Sum of the GPU elapsed time of individual H2D submission windows for that forward. |\\n\\nThe active payload is CD3 body rows, active Packed20 entry words and CSR\\noffsets; P4Flat's selected `total_size` values; or ZipServ's selected bitmap,\\noffset and variable payload sizes. Raw payloads have compression ratio 1.\\nRepeated loads count repeatedly: these are traffic-weighted ratios of the KV\\nbeing loaded, not an inventory of all KV stored in memory. Raw span coalescing\\ncan copy holes, so its transfer ratio need not be 1. Empty transfers have zero\\nbytes and an undefined (`NA`) ratio.\\n\\nTiming is enabled only by the suites' existing `--breakdown` option. Its begin\\nand end events bracket memcpy submission after host preparation and existing\\nbuffer dependencies. Decompression and preceding ring waits are excluded.\\nResource contention and exposed submission gaps inside the window remain\\nincluded. Windows on different streams can overlap; their sum is not an\\nadditive decomposition of GPU forward time or pure copy-engine activity.\\n`KVLoadResidualEstimate` preserves the old union-minus-weight calculation as a\\ndiagnostic only. `ExposedLoad` uses the new windows too and remains a window\\noverlap metric, not GPU idle time.\\n\\nCounters use CPU metadata and native copy descriptors. They do not copy sizes\\nback from the GPU or add synchronization. Event pairs and counter slots are\\nreused, including distinct slots for multiple chunks of one layer. CSV output\\noccurs once per completed host forward, not per layer. Timing readback never\\nwaits; unfinished timing is `NA`. Existing diagnostic breakdown synchronization\\nis unchanged. The offline CPU diagnostic CSV still exposes CD3 plan/native\\npreparation and staging costs separately.\\n\\nRaw, CD3, P4Flat (including its shared UBLB staging), and ZipServ paths are\\naccounted, including mixed prefill and raw fallbacks. Optional codecs without\\nbyte accounting produce `bytes_complete=0` and `NA`, never a fabricated zero.\\nSummary rows require complete coverage; `bytes_complete_forwards` and\\n`timed_forwards` expose missing data.\\n\\nSummaries group by config, offline batch and phase. Offline forward CSVs also\\ncarry the driver's step index. Summary byte sums include the recorded warmup\\nsteps; the existing offline GPU breakdown retains its own decode warmup\\nexclusion. Serving counters cover all recorded model forwards, including\\nstartup requests and the drain, and are not trimmed to the client's request\\ncohort. They must not be divided by trimmed client token totals.\\n\\nFor direct runner use, set `TIERED_SERVE_KV_METRICS=1` and\\n`TIERED_SERVE_KV_METRICS_DIR=/path/to/output`. `TIERED_SERVE_COLLECT_TIME=1`\\nalso enables event timing. Updated native bindings are built by the existing\\nextension loader on the next launch; allow for the first-launch rebuild.\\n\"}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":1,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"171285\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000002496,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":140,\"output\":\"_offline_staged_correctness.py\\ncpp_extensions/csrc/include/kv_compress_worker.hpp\\ncpp_extensions/csrc/include/unload_worker.hpp\\ncpp_extensions/csrc/unload_worker_ext.cpp\\noffline_offload_kvweight.py\\npatches/vllm-flash-attn.patch\\npatches/vllm.patch\\nscripts/offline/run_performance_suite.sh\\nscripts/serving/client/offline_throughput.sh\\ntests/test_kv_cpu_profile.py\\ntests/test_kv_free_breakdown.py\\ntiered_serve/compression/adapters/zipserv/kv_c